################################################################################
# NOTES FOR CROSS-CONTROLLER TESTING
################################################################################
#
# IMPORTANT TESTING GUIDELINES:
#
# 1. ENTITY RELATIONSHIPS:
#    - Person is independent (no FK required)
#    - ContactInfo requires PersonId (Foreign Key)
#    - Address requires ContactInfoId (Foreign Key)
#
# 2. TESTING ORDER:
#    - Always create in this order: Person → Contact → Address
#    - Always delete in reverse order: Address → Contact → Person
#    - Never delete a parent before deleting children
#
# 3. ID MANAGEMENT:
#    - IDs are auto-generated and sequential
#    - First Person gets ID: 1
#    - First Contact gets ID: 1
#    - First Address gets ID: 1
#    - When creating Contact, use PersonId returned from Person POST
#    - When creating Address, use ContactInfoId returned from Contact POST
#
# 4. FOREIGN KEY VALIDATION:
#    - Creating Contact with invalid PersonId → 400 Bad Request
#    - Creating Address with invalid ContactInfoId → 400 Bad Request
#    - System enforces referential integrity
#
# 5. EXPECTED HTTP STATUS CODES:
#    - 200 OK      : Successful GET, PUT, DELETE
#    - 201 Created : Successful POST (returns Location header)
#    - 400 Bad Request : Invalid FK, missing fields, bad data
#    - 404 Not Found : Resource doesn't exist
#    - 500 Server Error : Unexpected error
#
# 6. KAFKA EVENT PROCESSING:
#    - Each POST/PUT/DELETE triggers Kafka event
#    - Events are processed asynchronously
#    - Check Consumer logs for workflow execution
#    - Workflow validates all related data
#
# 7. WORKFLOW VALIDATION:
#    - PersonWorkflow validates Person, Contacts, and Addresses
#    - Step 1: ValidatePersonStep - checks Person data
#    - Step 2: ValidateContactStep - checks Contact data
#    - Step 3: ValidateAddressStep - checks Address data
#    - All steps run in sequence for each event
#
# 8. TESTING BEST PRACTICES:
#    - Run requests in order (top to bottom)
#    - Note returned IDs from POST responses
#    - Use those IDs in subsequent requests
#    - Test positive cases first, then error cases
#    - Always clean up created data
#    - Check that FK relationships are enforced
#    - Verify cascading effects
#
# 9. PAYLOAD VALIDATION:
#    Person:
#    - firstName: required (string)
#    - lastName: required (string)
#    - dateOfBirth: optional (ISO date)
#
#    ContactInfo:
#    - email: required (valid email format)
#    - phone: required (string)
#    - personId: required (valid Person ID)
#    - type: optional (enum)
#
#    Address:
#    - street: required (string)
#    - city: required (string)
#    - state: required (string)
#    - postalCode: required (string)
#    - country: optional (string, default: USA)
#    - addressType: optional (enum)
#    - contactInfoId: required (valid ContactInfo ID)
#
# 10. TROUBLESHOOTING:
#    - 404 on Contact creation: Verify Person exists
#    - 404 on Address creation: Verify Contact exists
#    - 400 on Contact/Address: Check FK IDs are valid
#    - Kafka not processing: Ensure Consumer service is running
#    - Slow responses: Check database and network connectivity
#
################################################################################
